PotatoVillain@gmail.com wrote:
> I've been playing nethack for a few years off and on, and never
> really gotten a character past level 8, so my recent death in the
> astral plane was an extremely big leap forward for me. Be warned, this
> post is pretty long, and contains spoilers.

I feel the need to point out all your mistakes, so you do better next
time.

Note that I haven't gotten a character past level 8 either (outside of
Explore/Wizard mode), so you don't have to take my advice...

> [...] started engrave-testing wands. Imagine my surprise
> when the following comes up: "You may wish for any item."
> Determined not to screw this up, I looked up a wishing spoiler and
> studied it carefully. My first wish netted me one blessed scroll of
> charging (I asked for two). My second and third (yes, three! How
> fortunate!) wishes were for a SDSM and gauntlets of power, both with +2
> enchants. Thinking I was a clever person, I zapped my empty wand until
> I got another wish, and cooked up a cloak of magic resist. The wand
> then disintegrated, and I realized what I had done. This was mistake
> #1.

No, mistake #1 was not wishing for the Eyes of the Overworld. A Valk
with an early wand of wishing is nearly invincible, unless they make
some YASD (which they probably will). Anyway, the point is, if you have
more than 40 HP, wish for the Eyes. If you don't, wait until you do,
then wish for the Eyes. They grant MR, removing the need for the CoMR,
they give unlimited enlightenment (which is useful for IDing rings),
and they give astral vision and make you unable to be blinded, which is
a big plus.

> [..] Next I headed to Sokoban. [...] a grey unicorn got stuck
> behind a boulder and I had to kill it. Unfortunately, I couldn't kill it
> without my gear so I decided to break the boulder and then kill it,
> since it was already hostile.

Without your gear? What do you mean? You should find anything to throw
and throw it at the unicorn if it's already hostile. Never break a
boulder in Soko unless you absolutely must.

> I started to descend deeper, my bags brimming with
> unidentified crap (even wands - very dangerous).

Engrave-ID all wands, and only put ones in your bag that you're sure
aren't cancellation.

> I zapped a wand and it changed the engraving to some
> fortune, so clearly this is a wand of enlightenment.

As someone else pointed out, you mean polymorph.

> I zap myself and bam - I'm a silver dragon. It's kind of cool, but I was
> weaker, and my cloak broke.

Another advantage of the Eyes.

> At this point, I was still struggling with unidentified scrolls,
> potions, rings, and wands.

Engrave-ID wands. They're the easiest to ID.

> [...] I went in and sat on the throne.
> Unfortunately, this cursed one of my bags of holding, and I had to
> evacuate it's contents to the other bag and dump it.

This is definitely avoidable. Check the spoilers.

Also, items can randomly disappear from cursed bags of holding if you
use them. At this point, you should have backup holy water in your sack
for emergencies like this.

> Maze after maze gets really
> boring, and with uncontrolled teleportitis, really annoying.

How did uncontrolled teleportitis happen? If you have it and any wishes
at all, a wish for a ring of teleport control is necessary (or two tins
of tengu meat, if you're feeling lucky).

> [...] until I came to Asmodeus'
> lair. I got the honor of fighting him and Baezulbub at the same time.
> After a very long fight and something blinding me, [...]

Yet another advantage of the Eyes.

> But now with -17 AC and a +4 superhammer, I'm at
> the valley of the dead and ready to get the amulet.

No, you are not, you are ready to burn a few more wishes on magic
markers and get your hammer to +6/7, a katana (or longsword or silver
saber, depending on availability and preference) to twoweapon to +6/7,
and all your armor to +4/5, and rust/fireproofed.

And alch for potions of full healing, to get your max HP up to a
reasonable level. Or, at the very least, bless all the potions of full
healing you've found so far and drink them (not all of them - save a
few for emergencies).

> I'm working my way up Rodney's tower, and I see a master mind
> flayer. Thinking I am invincible, I attack it and it mind-sucks me.

NEVER melee a mind flayer, whether or not your are invincible. Know
that well.

> [...] About halfway up through hell, I walk through a door and
> am hit by a potion of paralysis. It was thrown by a master mind flayer.

Did I mention that a wish for a ring of free action is a really good
idea if you don't have one by the ascension run?

> [...] I find my altar, sacrifice and pray, but Odin doesn't
> even uncurse any of my stuff. I replace my cursed unicorn horn, and
> continue on. [...]

Do you not have holy water? Check the spoilers - you definitely should,
and you should never let your unihorn become uncursed very long, let
alone cursed.

> [...] Plane of Earth [...] start searching. Finding
> the portal wasn't too bad,

This is what scrolls of gold detection are for. Carry a few for the
Planes.

Oh, and, side note: If you didn't realize, now's a good time to pitch
your ring of tele control, since you're not going to be using it again,
and you'll need the ring slot.

> [...] Hey there's Death. He gets
> dropped in three hits, what a chump. My angel and I start clearing the
> first left room. Death gets up and I kill him again - wait, what? I
> only have 93 max hit points now.

You shouldn't melee Death unless you have to. Throw daggers or Mojo if
you're feeling lucky, zap wands, boulder fortress if you have lots of
free time.

Also, this is why alching for FH potions is such a good idea - your max
hit points would be 400 instead of 93.

